## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cost-aware, privacy-preserving on-device ML feature with hardware constraints and OTA workflows.

## Key Concepts
- On-device graph neural networks
- Privacy-preserving data handling
- OTA delta updates
- Drift detection and validation
- ECU hardware constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code snippet for delta update application
function applyDelta(model, delta) {
  // merge weights with low-precision quantization
  for (let i=0; i<model.length; i++) model[i] = saturate(model[i] + delta[i], -128, 127);
  return model;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy and security in OTA payload?
- How to handle drift when sensors drop or fail to report?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about data integrity, offline-first design, and privacy/compliance trade-offs in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- offline-first data modeling
- tamper-evident logs (hash chaining)
- delta synchronization with encryption
- data retention and regulatory considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal hash chain for integrity check
function hashChain(entries) {
  let h = 0;
  for (const e of entries) h = (hashfunc(e) ^ h) >>> 0;
  return h;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model storage budget over 12 months?
- What are failure modes if delta sync fails or duplicates?

## Why This Is Asked
Privacy-preserving on-device experiments enable rapid iteration without raw data leaving devices, aligning with regulatory scrutiny and low-latency user experience goals.

## Key Concepts
- On-device flag evaluation and cohort management
- Local storage and memory budgeting
- Delta-based telemetry with minimal data exposure
- Safe rollout, rollback, and veto mechanisms
- Compliance and auditability considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Local flag evaluation snippet (pseudo)
function evalFlag(user, flagRepo) {
  const cohort = user.cohortId;
  const flag = flagRepo.getFlag(cohort);
  return flag.evaluate(user);
}
```

